## Root Cause
In ScrollablePanel.cs line 255-267, OnShown has a try-catch that silently swallows exceptions:
```csharp
protected override void OnShown(EventArgs e)
{
    if (Loaded) {
        try {
            fViewport = UIHelper.Rt2Rt(VisibleRect);
            UpdateProperties();
        } catch {
            // FIXME: works in MacOS and doesn't work in Wpf
        }
    }
    base.OnShown(e);
}
```

The VisibleRect property works on macOS (NSScrollView provides it) but throws on WPF. The catch block masks the WPF failure silently.

## Fix
Add platform detection to use the correct viewport calculation method per platform:
- macOS: Use VisibleRect (works correctly via NSScrollView)
- WPF: Use an alternative approach to calculate viewport (e.g., ActualWidth/ActualHeight or ScrollViewer properties)
- Remove the blanket try-catch

## Files to Change
- projects/GKv3/GKComponents/GKUI/Components/ScrollablePanel.cs lines 255-267

## Verification
- Scroll behavior works on macOS without exceptions
- Scroll behavior works on WPF without exceptions
- No silent error swallowing
